{"text": "ANDREW A. MORRIS\n\nMoberly, MO 65270\n\n1 C_C_|\nee \u2014\u2014OeeQQeESE=Eeeeee\nCAREER SUMMARY\n\nEstablished background in municipal government, management, economic\ndevelopment, grant and loan solicitation, personnel administration and governmental\n\nrelations.\n\nEDUCATION\n\nMaster of Arts in Business 1998\nWebster University, St. Louis, Missouri\n\nMaster of Public Administration 1987\n\u2018Arkansas State University, Jonesboro, Arkansas\n\nBachelor of Arts in Political Science 1986\nOttawa University, Ottawa, Kansas\nStudent Body President\n\nCAREER EXPERIENCE\nCity of Moberly, Missouri 2007 - Present\nCity Manager\n\u2018Administrative head of local government, oversee municipal operations including administration\nfinance, personnel, public utilities, public works, police and fire.\nAccomplishments:\n= Streamlined the budget process, reduced fund transfers and established to general fund reserve\npolicy.\nCreated neighborhood associations in our community to serve the needs of low to moderate\nincome residents, by coordinating public and private resources to improve neighborhoods.\n= Developed a schedule to invest certain fund balances in storm water and street projects.\nInitiated a staffing analysis, and used the results to create a more efficient city staff by\nconsolidating certain department operations and positions.\nDeveloped an employee engagement survey that has resulted in tangible communication efforts\nbetween management and staff.\n\nCity of Ottumwa, Iowa 2006 - 2007\nCity Administrator\n\u2018Administrative head of local government, oversee municipal operations including finance,\npersonnel, solid waste, sanitary sewers, planning, public safety, and intergovernmental relations.\nAccomplishments:\n= Renegotiated event center contract, saving the city $285,000.\nSuccessfully negotiated employee bargaining agreements with Teamsters.\n= Streamlined personnel in the City Engineer's office, resulting in a savings of $65,000.",
